#### Step 3: Add `toml_value_to_yaml_value` conversion function

**File**: `/private/var/folders/_q/qzh8_t6s15388qqf3p6n3d200000gp/T/bench-uji3m3e6/src/config/loader.rs` (or a new `src/config/format.rs` module if preferred for separation -- but keeping it in `loader.rs` is simpler given the scope)

```rust
/// Convert a `toml::Value` into a `serde_yaml::Value`.
///
/// This allows TOML-parsed configuration to enter the same
/// merge pipeline that YAML configs use.
fn toml_value_to_yaml_value(value: &toml::Value) -> serde_yaml::Value {
    match value {
        toml::Value::String(s) => serde_yaml::Value::String(s.clone()),
        toml::Value::Integer(i) => serde_yaml::Value::Number(serde_yaml::Number::from(*i)),
        toml::Value::Float(f) => {
            serde_yaml::Value::Number(serde_yaml::Number::from(*f))
        }
        toml::Value::Boolean(b) => serde_yaml::Value::Bool(*b),
        toml::Value::Datetime(dt) => {
            // TOML datetimes have no direct YAML equivalent; store as string
            serde_yaml::Value::String(dt.to_string())
        }
        toml::Value::Array(arr) => {
            serde_yaml::Value::Sequence(
                arr.iter().map(toml_value_to_yaml_value).collect()
            )
        }
        toml::Value::Table(table) => {
            let mut mapping = serde_yaml::Mapping::new();
            for (key, val) in table {
                mapping.insert(
                    serde_yaml::Value::String(key.clone()),
                    toml_value_to_yaml_value(val),
                );
            }
            serde_yaml::Value::Mapping(mapping)
        }
    }
}
```

Key design notes:
- `toml::Value::Datetime` maps to a YAML string since YAML has no native datetime scalar type (and `BivvyConfig` fields that accept dates, like `chrono::DateTime`, will parse from string via serde anyway).
- `toml::Value::Integer` is `i64`, which maps directly to `serde_yaml::Number::from(i64)`.
- `toml::Value::Float` is `f64`, mapping to `serde_yaml::Number::from(f64)`.

