#### Step 6: Modify `parse_config` and `load_config_file` for TOML

**File**: `/private/var/folders/_q/qzh8_t6s15388qqf3p6n3d200000gp/T/bench-uji3m3e6/src/config/loader.rs`

`parse_config` (line 161) and `load_config_file` (line 141) are used for the `--config` override path (see `load_config` at line 252). These need TOML support too.

```rust
/// Parse config content into BivvyConfig, detecting format from the source path extension.
pub fn parse_config(content: &str, source_path: &Path) -> Result<BivvyConfig> {
    let format = ConfigFormat::from_path(source_path).unwrap_or(ConfigFormat::Yaml);

    match format {
        ConfigFormat::Yaml => {
            serde_yaml::from_str(content).map_err(|e| BivvyError::ConfigParseError {
                path: source_path.to_path_buf(),
                message: e.to_string(),
            })
        }
        ConfigFormat::Toml => {
            toml::from_str(content).map_err(|e| BivvyError::ConfigParseError {
                path: source_path.to_path_buf(),
                message: e.to_string(),
            })
        }
    }
}
```

Note: For `parse_config` in the TOML case, we can deserialize directly from TOML into `BivvyConfig` using `toml::from_str` because `BivvyConfig` derives `Deserialize` via serde, which is format-agnostic. No need for the conversion step here since there is no merging involved.

`load_config_file` calls `parse_config`, so it needs no additional changes -- it already passes the path through.

