#### Step 9: Update `init.rs` for TOML awareness

**File**: `/private/var/folders/_q/qzh8_t6s15388qqf3p6n3d200000gp/T/bench-uji3m3e6/src/cli/commands/init.rs`

The `config_exists()` method (line 46) only checks for `config.yml`. It should also check for `config.toml`:

```rust
fn config_exists(&self) -> bool {
    self.project_root.join(".bivvy/config.yml").exists()
        || self.project_root.join(".bivvy/config.toml").exists()
}
```

The init command currently always writes YAML (line 258). This is fine -- `init` creates YAML by default. A future enhancement could add `--format toml` but that is out of scope for this change. The important thing is that `config_exists()` prevents `init` from overwriting an existing TOML config without `--force`.

The `.gitignore` update (line 143) currently adds `.bivvy/config.local.yml`. It should also add `.bivvy/config.local.toml`:

```rust
fn update_gitignore(&self, ui: &mut dyn UserInterface) -> Result<()> {
    let entries = [".bivvy/config.local.yml", ".bivvy/config.local.toml"];
    let gitignore_path = self.project_root.join(".gitignore");

    if gitignore_path.exists() {
        let content = fs::read_to_string(&gitignore_path)?;
        let mut new_content = content.clone();
        let mut added = false;

        for entry in &entries {
            if !new_content.contains(entry) {
                if !new_content.ends_with('\n') {
                    new_content.push('\n');
                }
                new_content.push_str(entry);
                new_content.push('\n');
                added = true;
            }
        }

        if added {
            fs::write(&gitignore_path, new_content)?;
            ui.message("Added .bivvy/config.local.{yml,toml} to .gitignore");
        }
    }

    Ok(())
}
```

